Spec written and self-review fixes applied at `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-15-v1.1-checkpoints-custom-ref-design.md` (not committed, per your instruction). The targeted fixes:

- corrected the `metadata.json` byte-identical claim — the two refs' summaries agree on shared fields but diverge on `Sessions[].Transcript` / `Sessions[].ContentHash`;
- corrected the blob-deduplication claim — only `prompt.txt` and similar transcript-agnostic sidecars share blobs;
- committed to specific function names for the `writeCommittedV2` split (`writeCompactRef` always-on; `writeCommittedV2FullIfEnabled` gated);
- scoped the lazy on-demand fetch of the compact ref to the same commands that already do this for the legacy branch (notably `entire resume <id>`), not every read;
- dropped the redundant compile-time-assertion bullet (the `V2MainRefName = MetadataCompactRefName` alias is already the assertion).

Please review the spec and let me know if you want any changes before I hand off to writing-plans.

